title: Installing an Importer
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

The recipient's wiki has nothing installed, so download the combined
file: ''Download pack + runtime'' saves `invoice-importer-with-runtime.json`.

# Open an empty TiddlyWiki (a fresh `empty.html` from tiddlywiki.com will do).
# Drag the downloaded file onto it.  The import dialog lists two plugins: ''JSON Convert'' (the runtime) and ''Invoice Importer''.  Both are ticked; click ''Import''.
# Save the wiki and reload it, as TiddlyWiki asks after any plugin with JavaScript arrives.

''Screenshot needed:'' the import dialog in the empty wiki listing the
two plugins.

After the reload, ''More › Importers'' in the sidebar lists ''Import
Invoices''.  The control panel's plugin list shows ''Invoice Importer''
with its readme: what it does, a link to the page, the fields it
expects, and where it came from.

''Screenshot needed:'' ''More › Importers'' showing the one entry.

!!! A wiki that already has the runtime

If the recipient already has JSON Convert -- another importer, say --
''Download pack'' gives a smaller file with just the importer.  The
combined file is safe there too: TiddlyWiki keeps the installed runtime
when the incoming one is the same version or older, and takes only the
pack.

!!! Without the runtime

If someone drags in a pack alone, without the runtime, the page does
not fail silently.  It shows one sentence: which plugin is missing, and
a link to fetch it from the studio that made the importer.
